  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Borderland Ghana - Strengthening the Resilience of Border Communities in Bounkani to Reduce Vulnerability and Prevent Conflict</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall aim of the project is to reduce farmer-herder conflicts and strengthen the resilience of border communities in the face of vulnerabilities linked to access to natural resources and basic social services, particularly water. This will be achieved by strengthening community mechanisms and state structures, promoting the active participation of communities in conflict prevention, and improving access to drinking water services, sustainable livelihoods and agro-pastoral resources. The project will focus on indigenous peoples, migrants, adolescents, young people, women, displaced persons/asylum seekers, pastoralists, farmers and agro-pastoralists, in order to promote inclusive dialogue and strengthen social cohesion within communities. At the same time, the intervention and coordination capacities of local and national government structures will be strengthened to improve conflict prevention and management. All of the interventions under this project will be carried out in coordination and complementarity with the national and international institutions working in the Bounkani region on the issues addressed. Specifically, the project will work with GIZ, which is setting up local agro-pastoral management committees (CLGA) to facilitate concerted management of natural resources as part of the Pr2GRN project, which is funded by BMZ and the EU.</narrative>
  </description>
